      "prompt": "Draw exactly ONE original Small Seal glyph from the attached four-specimen reference. Inspect all available THX CCZ QJZ DYC specimens; choose coherent whole THX construction, no blending variants. Rounded Gothic sans-serif MONOLINE, absolutely constant stroke width about 3% canvas, round caps and joins, smooth curves, no taper or brush or serif. Faithful connections, separate strokes and counters. Center glyph within central 70% square canvas. Pure BLACK on fully TRANSPARENT background. No labels, grids, text or multiple glyphs. Two detached top tridents. Beneath TWO separate parallel slanted rounded loop forms stacked vertically. Each is curved top rail sweeping up-right, rounding at right then returning down-left as long diagonal; one short inner diagonal joins top rail to lower return, makes ONE small upperrightcounter. Topform lowerlefttail ends above lowerform, lowerform tail longer reaches baseline. Two counters total, no vertical joining forms.",
